course: dictionary
lesson: 4494
title: Proud and looking down
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what a character is like inside, not just what they do. Haughty is one of these. It means proud and unfriendly, as if you are better than other people. «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall» is a warning in the Bible: a proud spirit is a bad thing to have.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. In a story, a haughty character often looks down on others, speaks in a cold voice, or ignores people who are not important to them. In «a haughty look», the look is not friendly. It says, I am better than you.
explain: In «Man-who-turns-his-back-on-callers», the Stranger-man thinks the chief must be haughty because he never turns round to greet visitors. The clue is the rudeness, not a word that says haughty. Readers have to work it out from what the character does.
fact: Haughty means proud and unfriendly, acting as if you are better than other people.
fact: «A haughty look» means a look that shows someone thinks they are better than others.
fact: Haughty is often used for snobbish characters, such as queens, princesses or rich people in stories.
fact: Haughty is a feeling and a behaviour: the character is proud inside, and it shows in how they act.
fact: Haughty is not the same as happy or kind. It usually suggests coldness or rudeness.
exercise: «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall.» What does haughty mean? | *Proud and unfriendly, looking down on others | Kind and gentle to everyone | Very tired after a long day | Frightened of the dark
exercise: Why does the Stranger-man think the chief is haughty? | Because he has a bright red hat | Because it is raining | Because he is singing a happy song | *Because he never turns round to greet callers
exercise: «The haughty queen would not speak to the farmers.» Find and copy the word that shows the queen looks down on others. | farmers | queen | speak | *haughty
test: «The haughty queen would not speak to the farmers.» What does haughty show about the queen? | *Pride and looking down on others | Kindness | Fear of the rain | Tiredness
test: Tom says a haughty voice is a friendly voice. Is he right? | *No, a haughty voice sounds proud and unfriendly | Yes, because haughty means warm and cheerful | No, because haughty means very loud | Yes, because haughty means quiet
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to haughty? | *Proud | Humble | Cheerful | Shy
